            ("The ingredients", "A strong temperature contrast between the cold land air and the warm Gulf Stream; a jet stream that provides divergence aloft; and release of latent heat as water vapour condenses. The storm feeds on moisture from the sea, so heating by condensation can account for half of the deepening."),
            ("Famous cases", "The 'Storm of the Century' of March 1993 on the US East Coast; the 'bomb cyclone' of January 2018 along the same coast; and the remnants of Typhoon Nuri in November 2014, which exploded in the Bering Sea to one of the most intense storms on record there, with a central pressure near 924 hPa."),
