            "A flash is about 30,000 °C, five times hotter than the surface of the Sun. It heats the air so fast that the air expands explosively, making a shock wave that you hear as **thunder**. Light travels almost instantly, but sound takes about 3 seconds to cover each kilometre, so counting the seconds between flash and bang tells you how far away it is.",
